  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The reported experimental findings reflect a single initial run per configuration designed primarily to demonstrate platform functionality rather than a comprehensive empirical study of policy impacts.",
      "what": "The authors developed AgenticMobility, an open-source framework that integrates persistent large language model agents with the MATSim traffic simulator to model interactions between dynamic travelers and transport managers. In an initial test spanning five configurations over 100 simulated days, the system successfully executed 1,179,300 constraint-compliant travel decisions, demonstrating stable route preferences alongside adapting departure times in response to automated link-charge adjustments.",
      "why": "It enables researchers to test how self-directed, LLM-based agents adapt through repeated exposure to policy interventions, moving beyond static rule-based behavioral models in multi-agent traffic simulations."
    }
  },
